# Time-blocking system (simplified version)

# Focus: minimal interruptions, single daily cutoff, no forced mid-day breaks

# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Night protection: prevent PC usage during sleep hours

# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Ensures system is not used during late night / sleep window

0 0-6 * * * root /sbin/shutdown

# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Daily end of work: 21:30 shutdown

# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Main discipline rule: end of productive day

30 21 * * * root /sbin/shutdown

# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Weekend rule (optional but consistent cutoff)

# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Keeps rhythm stable across week; removes "infinite weekend usage"

30 21 * * Sat root /sbin/shutdown
30 21 * * Sun root /sbin/shutdown

# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional safety layer (soft enforcement instead of instant shutdown)

# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Locks session shortly before shutdown (gives warning effect)

25 21 * * * root /usr/bin/loginctl lock-sessions

# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Notes:

# - Removed all lunch / mid-day shutdown blocks

# - Removed phone-related logic entirely

# - Removed fragmented time-block enforcement (simplified to one anchor point)

# - System now relies on:

# 1) Night cutoff (sleep protection)

# 2) Single daily shutdown (discipline boundary)

# 3) Optional lock warning (transition buffer)
